 "preferred_name": "Rubber-tyred metro",
 "kind": "knowledge",
 "definition": "A metro system whose trains run on rubber tyres on concrete or steel guideways instead of steel wheels on steel rails.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A form of rapid transit that mixes road and rail technology, with rubber-tyred wheels running on a roll way between guide bars. Steel flanged wheels on rails guide it through switches and act as backup if tyres fail. Most such trains are purpose-built for their system.",
